    "text": "A cylinder containing an ideal gas ( <math><mn>0.1</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi></math> of <math><mn>1.0</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></math> ) is in thermal equilibrium with a large volume of <math><mn>0.5</mn></math> molal aqueous solution of ethylene glycol at its freezing point. If the stoppers <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></math> and <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></math> (as shown in the figure) are suddenly withdrawn, the volume of the gas in litres after equilibrium is achieved will be _____________.<br />(Given, <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">f</mi></mrow></msub><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">w</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>2.0</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><mfenced open=\"\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.08</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi>